WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.379 --> 00:00:07.519
Breaking Bad is arguably one of the best and
most talked about shows ever. But while the

00:00:07.519 --> 00:00:11.780
principal cast have mostly all gone on to
high visibility projects, some of the actors

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:15.680
who played minor roles have had trouble finding
their way out of the ABQ.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.090
Julia Minesci

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:21.519
Julia Minesci landed the role of Wendy, Jesse's
customer and occasional paramour-for-hire,

00:00:21.519 --> 00:00:25.599
only as a result of a "midlife crisis, turning
fifty" thing, according to an interview she

00:00:25.599 --> 00:00:30.659
did with AMC. She was so convincing as a prostitute
that a guy supposedly drove up and tried to

00:00:30.659 --> 00:00:34.360
proposition her while they were shooting a
scene for the show. Unfortunately, Breaking

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:38.300
Bad wasn't the career catapult she thought
it might be. With only one other short film

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.650
credit to her name in the six years since
she started the show, her turn as the root

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:45.630
beer and meth-loving hooker of The Crosswinds
Motel may have turned out to be just a flash

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:46.670
in the pan.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:48.060
Marius Stan

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:52.790
After playing Walter White's mean boss Bogdan
at the A1A Car Wash, Marius Stan hasn't had

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:56.670
any acting work since Breaking Bad. But that's
okay—he's actually a real-life scientist

00:00:56.670 --> 00:01:01.040
with a PhD in Chemistry who works as a Senior
Computational Energy Scientist at Argonne

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:06.049
National Laboratory outside of Chicago. Probably
beats running a carwash.

00:01:06.049 --> 00:01:08.109
Lavell Crawford

00:01:08.109 --> 00:01:12.770
Comedian Lavell Crawford played Huell, who
was basically a one-joke character. As the

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:16.729
enforcer for crooked lawyer Saul Goodman,
he barely spoke a word on the show—but still

00:01:16.729 --> 00:01:21.469
managed to be hilarious in every scene. His
post-Breaking Bad credits don't boast much,

00:01:21.469 --> 00:01:25.229
but they do include roles in American Ultra
and the Adam Sandler movie The Ridiculous

00:01:25.229 --> 00:01:25.969
Six.

00:01:25.969 --> 00:01:27.630
RJ Mitte

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:31.799
Before becoming the breakfast-loving son of
Walter White, RJ Mitte had a kind of sporadic

00:01:31.799 --> 00:01:36.079
acting career, like a few background roles
in Hannah Montanna. He's since moved on to

00:01:36.079 --> 00:01:40.929
Switched at Birth, a series on ABC Family,
and landed a few movie roles. But we're still

00:01:40.929 --> 00:01:44.530
holding out for Mitte to land a cooking show
where he just makes breakfast every episode.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:48.590
Seriously, we'd binge-watch this guy eating
pancakes and eggs for hours.

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:49.850
Matt Jones

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:54.499
Landing a string of roles on network TV shows
like NCIS and Mom after Breaking Bad ended,

00:01:54.499 --> 00:01:57.889
Matt Jones first won our hearts as Badger,
Jesse's scratchy-voiced underling.

00:01:57.889 --> 00:01:59.259
"I wanna be a knight."

00:01:59.259 --> 00:02:02.999
These days, he's got the role of Pig on the
Nickelodeon show Pig Goat Banana Cricket.

00:02:02.999 --> 00:02:06.749
Man, first Badger, now Pig. Dude's like a
one-man zoo.

00:02:06.749 --> 00:02:08.259
Charles Baker

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:12.200
Skinny Pete was half of the comic relief duo
who sporadically showed up in various henchman

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:16.540
roles for both Jesse and Walter. Although
he played a spaced-out meth addict, Charles

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:20.680
Baker is actually a classically trained stage
performer and an accomplished pianist in real

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:23.940
life, as demonstrated by his beautiful playing
in the episode "Hazard Pay."

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:39.240
(piano playing)

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:40.560
"You sound great!"

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.410
After Breaking Bad, he did some work on mainstream
shows like NBC's The Blacklist, but he's since

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:48.590
turned his attention to independent film work
like the sci-fi thriller Approaching the Unknown

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:53.790
and Nicolas Winding Refn's 2016 film The Neon
Demon. Those are probably creatively fulfilling

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:57.680
projects for sure. But toss some of those
names out to a general audience and they're

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:00.860
going to look back at you like you just recited
Badger and Skinny Pete's Star Trek pitch:

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:06.520
"I'm on the Starship Enterprise mackin' on
Yeoman Rand while the Andorian with the disruptor

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:09.140
is back on Talos IV or whatever."

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:12.390
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:15.690
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know which Breaking Bad character you like

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:16.190
the most...

